\[\mathbf{curl}\,\phi=\left(\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x_{2}},-\frac{ \partial\phi}{\partial x_{1}}\right)\!,\] \[\operatorname{curl}\mathbf{v}=\frac{\partial v_{2}}{\partial x_{ 1}}-\frac{\partial v_{1}}{\partial x_{2}}\!.\]

When \(N=3\), we define the curl of a distribution \(\mathbf{v}\) of \(\mathcal{D}^{\prime}(\Omega)^{3}\) by

\[\mathbf{curl}\,\mathbf{v}=\left(\frac{\partial v_{3}}{\partial x_{2}}-\frac{ \partial v_{2}}{\partial x_{3}},\frac{\partial v_{1}}{\partial x_{3}}-\frac{ \partial v_{3}}{\partial x_{1}},\frac{\partial v_{2}}{\partial x_{1}}-\frac{ \partial v_{1}}{\partial x_{2}}\right)\!.\]

